Subject: [PATCH 8/8] cfft, mdct, filtbank: the AAC core's inverse transform four lanes at a time

VibeSDR patch for FAAD2 2.11.3 (the plain build VibeServer links for DAB+ audio, libfaad_dab.a). GPL-2.0-or-later,
as FAAD2. Written for VibeSDR, 2026-10-26; applied by vibeserver/linux/build-deps.sh and vibeserver/mac/build-deps.sh
in the order of faad2-patches/series. Measured on real off-air DAB+ unit logs (HE-AAC v2, 21 logs, 1909 s):
output against stock FAAD2 2.11.3 built with its own flags — see each header for the figures.

The AAC-LC core every DAB+ service runs (alone on a 48 kHz AAC-LC service, under SBR on HE-AAC): the radix-4 complex
FFT pass (passf4pos, along ido), the iMDCT's pre- and post-twiddles (faad_imdct), and the long window's overlap-add
(ifilter_bank) — four lanes per instruction with the stock products and sums; ifilter_bank's 8 KB scratch buffer is no
longer zeroed on every call (every window sequence's iMDCTs write all of it before it is read). Measured on a 60 s
48 kHz AAC-LC stereo stream (1024-sample frames): armhf guest instructions stock 1519 M -> 770 M (patch 1 + flags)
-> 537 M with this patch; output against stock max |diff| 3.0e-7, SNR 140.1 dB, level/spectrum/side-mid identical.

